      "writtenOn": "2023-08-15T21:17:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically, this *also* needs `/androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnitRunner` (or some `runner_class`) at the end, but while that makes the command happy, it doesn\u0027t run any tests:\n\n```\nTime: 0.001\n\nOK (0 tests)\n```\n\nI think that was a reference to running `aarectmodes` with the `gles` backend, back when we used SkQP to run GMs. (Which I think is no longer the case?)\n\nWhen I run the whole suite, I see output naming the tests like `unitTest_makeBackendTexture`. Swapping out \"gles_aarectmodes\" with \"unitTest_makeBackendTexture\" or \"makeBackendTexture\" had the same effect.\n\n**EDIT**: Aha! I noticed that `SkQPRunner.java` prepends `UnitTest_` to the test, and I have confirmed that I can run a single test with a command like\n```\nadb shell am instrument -e class \u0027org.skia.skqp.SkQPRunner#UnitTest_AbandonedContextImage\u0027 -w org.skia.skqp/androidx.test.runner.AndroidJUnitRunner\n```\n\n(Running the same command without \"UnitTest_\", as implied by this line, does not work.)",
